1
00:00:00,000 --> 00:00:01,380
Tonight, the moon disappears.

2
00:00:02,000 --> 00:00:02,720
Gone,

3
00:00:03,260 --> 00:00:04,440
what happens to us?

4
00:00:05,020 --> 00:00:06,580
I'll answer that at the very end,

5
00:00:06,760 --> 00:00:09,040
because first we need three smaller answers.

6
00:00:09,640 --> 00:00:10,220
Question one,

7
00:00:10,700 --> 00:00:11,820
would the oceans flood?

8
00:00:12,440 --> 00:00:13,160
No,

9
00:00:13,540 --> 00:00:18,180
the moon's pull stretches the oceans into a bulge and that bulge is most of the tide.

10
00:00:18,580 --> 00:00:20,420
Without it, only the sun pulls.

11
00:00:21,040 --> 00:00:22,540
Tides shrink to about a third.

12
00:00:23,480 --> 00:00:24,240
Question two,

13
00:00:24,800 --> 00:00:25,940
would nights go black?

14
00:00:26,680 --> 00:00:31,160
Every night becomes a new moon night and some animals tell time by moonlight.

15
00:00:31,780 --> 00:00:33,260
On the Great Barrier Reef,

16
00:00:33,600 --> 00:00:37,040
corals release their eggs together a few nights after a full moon.

17
00:00:37,520 --> 00:00:38,100
No moon,

18
00:00:38,500 --> 00:00:39,280
no calendar.

19
00:00:40,460 --> 00:00:41,260
Question three,

20
00:00:42,240 --> 00:00:43,520
would our days change?

21
00:00:44,040 --> 00:00:45,720
Right now, the moon is a brake.

22
00:00:46,000 --> 00:00:52,120
Its tides drag on Earth's spin, so the day grows about two thousandths of a second longer every century.

23
00:00:52,680 --> 00:00:55,160
Take the moon away and the brake is gone.

24
00:00:55,440 --> 00:00:57,600
The day stays 24 hours,

25
00:00:58,260 --> 00:00:59,040
smaller tides,

26
00:00:59,220 --> 00:01:00,040
darker nights,

27
00:01:00,440 --> 00:01:01,420
the same day.

28
00:01:02,040 --> 00:01:03,540
That's fine?

29
00:01:04,480 --> 00:01:07,720
Then why do scientists call the moon Earth's stabiliser?

30
00:01:08,060 --> 00:01:09,920
Because Earth spins like a top,

31
00:01:10,340 --> 00:01:12,080
tilted 23 and a half degrees.

32
00:01:12,840 --> 00:01:16,800
That tilt gives us seasons and the moon's pull holds it steady.

33
00:01:17,140 --> 00:01:20,240
It barely wobbles about one degree either way.

34
00:01:20,760 --> 00:01:22,900
Without the moon, the tilt can drift.

35
00:01:23,160 --> 00:01:27,280
One famous study found it could swing from zero to 85 degrees.

36
00:01:28,120 --> 00:01:32,640
Newer studies say less, but still tens of degrees over millions of years.

37
00:01:33,040 --> 00:01:33,880
At zero,

38
00:01:34,100 --> 00:01:35,400
no seasons at all.

39
00:01:35,620 --> 00:01:36,520
At 85,

40
00:01:36,880 --> 00:01:39,640
one pole faces the sun for half a year.

41
00:01:40,280 --> 00:01:40,900
Endless day,

42
00:01:41,380 --> 00:01:42,620
then endless night.

43
00:01:43,280 --> 00:01:45,580
So what happens if the moon vanishes tonight?

44
00:01:46,020 --> 00:01:46,500
Tonight,

45
00:01:46,960 --> 00:01:47,780
almost nothing.

46
00:01:48,120 --> 00:01:52,600
But our far future grandchildren would live on a planet that slowly forgets its seasons.

47
00:01:53,220 --> 00:01:53,620
Next,

48
00:01:54,060 --> 00:01:55,460
what if Earth stopped spinning?
